<title>TURKEY: Rebel Kurds kill four villagers.</title>
<headline>Rebel Kurds kill four villagers.</headline>
<dateline>DIYARBAKIR, Turkey 1997-07-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>Kurdish rebels on Monday attacked a village in Turkey's southeast, killing four locals and injuring eight, security officials said.</p>
<p>They said guerrillas of the Kurdistan Workers Party (PKK) had raided the village of Ilicalar in Bingol province in the early evening.</p>
<p>No independent confirmation was available.</p>
<p>More than 25,000 people have died in the 12-year-old conflict between Turkish security forces and the PKK fighting for autonomy or independence in the mainly Kurdish southeast.</p>
<p>STR</p>
